<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hersekzade Ahmed Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1459–<a href="/years/1517">1517</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hersekzade Ahmed Pasha was an Ottoman statesman and admiral, born a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stjepan-vukcic-kosaca">Stjepan Vukčić Kosača</a>, Herceg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-sava">Saint Sava</a>. Taken to the Ottoman court as a youth, he converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and married a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-ii">Sultan Bayezid II</a>. He served five times as grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> under Bayezid II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-i">Selim I</a>, and commanded in campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>.</p></div>
